  "title": "Erdős Problem #836",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $r\\geq 2$ and $G$ be a $r$-uniform hypergraph with chromatic number $3$ (that is, there is a $3$-colouring of the vertices of $G$ such that no edge is monochromatic).\nSuppose any two edges of $G$ have a non-empty intersection. Must $G$ contain $O(r^2)$ many vertices? Must there be two edges which meet in $\\gg r$ many vertices?",
